From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 12:25:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] test(chunks): cover full-height biome palette decoding

Upstream #466 now reads modern biome palettes across the full dimension
height. Keep packet regressions for zero, one and nine block sections,
both cache paths, repeated palettes and the trailing chest block entity.
Reading only the block section count shifts biome bytes into block entity
NBT and corrupts the resulting state.

The fixture reproduces errors from BDS 1.26.51.1 (protocol 2193). The
Dragonfly v0.11.5 network decoder also reads the full dimension range:
https://github.com/df-mc/dragonfly/blob/v0.11.5/server/world/chunk/decode.go

These tests retain the boundary coverage after the upstream fix. Native
inventory navigation remains a separate validation requirement.
---
